// EXPECT: [E019]
// ADJUDICATED 2026-09-08: [E019] "only partially initialised" rather than [E005] "use of
// uninitialized variable". The array HAS been written, at a[0]; what is unwritten is the
// element being read. The new engine distinguishes wholly-uninitialised from partially
// initialised, which is a more accurate account of the same rejection.
// Reading an element of an uninitialized array is caught (was silent garbage).
//
// ADJUDICATED 2026-09-08: the program did not test its own intent. It wrote `a[0] = 5` and
// then read `a[0]`, which is the element it had just initialised, so there was nothing
// unsound about it — the old engine rejected it only because it treats an array as
// uninitialised until a WHOLE-array value is stored. It now reads `a[1]`, which is genuinely
// never written. Both engines reject that: [E005] from the old one, [E019] "only partially
// initialised" from the new.
func main() i32 {
    var a i32[4]
    a[0] = 5
    return a[1]
}
